9679 0 obj
  << /ActualText (We identified several technical and interaction issues from the first test run that we want to improve in the next iteration\072\n\nMore noticeable lighting feedback\050The lighting response needs to be more visually obvious so the DJ can immediately perceive how their hand gestures are affecting the music tempo and the surrounding atmosphere\056\n\nSmoother tempo transitions during gesture control\050During the first prototype test\054 tempo changes felt too abrupt when the DJ attempted to slow down the music gradually\056 This happened because the YouTube playback speed control does not allow continuous adjustments\056\050For the next Wizard of Oz prototype\054 the operator behind the scenes will manually adjust the tempo in smaller incremental steps\054 continuously matching the DJ\031s hand movement until the gesture stops\056 This should create a smoother and more natural interaction\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 9680 0 R
     /Pg 8791 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

9680 0 obj
  << /K [ 9679 0 R ]
     /P 9685 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 8791 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
